# Ooda CLI — Command Reference

File: ooda/docs/commands.oot

The `ooda` binary is a thin router. Language verbs forward to `cli`. Drivers spawn `opm`/`lsp`/`mcp`/`tui`. Deprecated verbs (gen, bench, digest, health, eval, repl, sandbox, swarm) print a moved line and exit 2. See `docs/argv.oot` and `docs/dispatch.oot`.

## Forwarded: build cluster

### ooda build

Compile a `.oo` file with `oodac`.

```sh
ooda build src/main.oo --target llvm -O2 -o build/main
ooda build src/main.oo --release --lto
```

Caps: FsRead, FsWrite, Process, Env. Source: `cli/build/host_build.oo::run_oodac_build`. Positional: the `.oo` file. Flags: `--target`, `-o`, `-O0..-O3`, `-Oz`, `-Opgo`, `--lto`, `--release`, `--pgo-generate`, `--pgo-use=`, `-fsanitize=`, `--fuzz`. Unknown flags fail closed. Exit: 0 ok; 2 missing/bad; 1 subprocess failure.

### ooda run

Compile and run a `.oo` file.

```sh
ooda run src/main.oo
```

Caps: FsRead, FsWrite, Process, Env. Source: `cli/build/host_build.oo::run_oodac_run`. `--engine=bc` is residual and exits 2. Exit: 0 ok; 2 residual/missing; 1 run failure.

### ooda gen

Moved. The router prints a moved line naming `opm gen <Kind> <Name>` and exits 2.

### ooda test

Compile and run a single `.oo` test file. Emits real JSON on `--json`.

```sh
ooda test tests/test_main.oo
ooda test tests/test_main.oo --engine=bc --json
```

Caps: FsRead, FsWrite, Process, Env, Time. Source: `cli/build/test.oo::run_ooda_test`. Flags: `--engine=bc` / `-bc`, `--json` / `-json`. Exit: 0 pass; 1 fail; 2 missing/unknown.

### ooda install

Install a pre-built openOODA release pack into an XDG prefix. Requires `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR`.

```sh
ooda install --from ./build/pack --to $HOME
ooda install            # uses OODA_CHECKOUT, OODA_FS_WRITEDIR
```

Caps: FsRead, FsWrite, Process, Env. Source: `cli/build/install.oo::run_ooda_install_cmd`. Flags: `--from <path>`, `--to <path>`. Exit: 0 ok; 1 bad path or non-pack.

### ooda update

Fetch the canonical `install.sh` and exec it to update the toolchain in place. This is the `ooda update` entry point the installer docs point at.

```sh
ooda update
ooda update --dry-run
ooda update --yes --no-modify-shell
ooda update --installer ./install.sh --dry-run
```

Caps: FsRead, Process, Env. Source: `cli/build/update.oo::run_ooda_update`. Flags: `--yes`, `--dry-run`, `--no-modify-shell`, `--installer <path>` (local script for offline use; `OODA_INSTALLER` is the env fallback). Default source is `https://openooda.org/install.sh` via `bash -c "set -o pipefail; curl ... | bash -s -- <flags>"` (pipefail so a dead download fails closed instead of execing an empty script). The fetch runs in a spawned child, so it needs child-process DNS; in locked-down sandboxes without it, download `install.sh` yourself and pass `--installer <path>`. Exit: 0 ok; 2 bad argv or unsafe installer path; 1 installer missing or failed.

### ooda bench

Moved. The router prints a moved line naming `bb bench <file>` and exits 2.

### ooda init

Bootstrap a new project layout (src/, tests/, ooda.pkg).

```sh
ooda init myapp
ooda init               # uses "myproject"
```

Caps: FsRead, FsWrite. Source: `cli/build/init.oo::cli_init_project`. Positional: project name (default `myproject`). Exit: 0 ok; 1 bad name or existing path.

### ooda context

List `.oo` files under a path, or stream the AI codex to stdout.

```sh
ooda context .
ooda context src --json
ooda context --llm
```

Caps: FsRead. Source: `cli/context.oo::run_ooda_context`. Positional: optional dir (default `.`). Flags: `--llm` (stream codex), `--json` (JSON listing). Exit: 0 ok.

### ooda health

Moved. The router prints a moved line naming `bb health` and exits 2.

## Forwarded: fix cluster

### ooda fix

Check a file, then apply at most 8 edits of kind E_CAP, E_TC, E_PARSE, E_IMP, or E_MUST. Write requires `--yes`.

```sh
ooda fix src/main.oo --dry-run
ooda fix src/main.oo --yes
```

Caps: FsRead, FsWrite, Process, Env. Source: `cli/fix/fix.oo::run_ooda_fix`. Flags: `--dry-run`, `--yes`. Exit: 0 ok; 1 no `--yes` or no supported diag; 2 bad path.

### ooda digest

Moved. The router prints a moved line naming `bb digest <file>` and exits 2.

## Forwarded: fmt cluster

### ooda fmt

Format `.oo` files in place under strict idempotence and cap audit.

```sh
ooda fmt src/main.oo
ooda fmt --all
ooda fmt --check src/main.oo
```

Caps: FsRead, FsWrite, Alloc. Source: `cli/fmt/fmt.oo::run_ooda_fmt`. Flags: `--check`, `--all`. Exit: 0 clean/rewrite; non-zero on bad file, missing cap, or non-idempotent.

## Forwarded: token cluster

### ooda token

Run a capability-token sub-subcommand. JSON is the default; `--human` switches to human-readable.

```sh
ooda token status
ooda token status --human
ooda token report
ooda token audit src/main.oo
ooda token query --baseline=v0.210
ooda token ask "what is the efficiency baseline?"
ooda token schema
ooda token diff before.oo after.oo
ooda token tail --lines=20
ooda token fix src/main.oo
ooda token snapshot
ooda token enforce
ooda token extra
```

Caps: FsRead, FsWrite, Process, Time. Source: `cli/token.oo::run_cli_token`. Positional: sub-subcommand name. Flags: `--human` / `-h`, `--format=human`, `--format=json`. Exit: 0 ok; sub-subcommand-defined.

The 12 sub-subcommands: `status`, `report`, `audit`, `query`, `ask`, `schema`, `diff`, `tail`, `fix`, `snapshot`, `enforce`, `extra`. Forwarded by `cli/token.oo`.

## Spawned: external packages

These spawn a subprocess and inherit stdio. The ooda binary does not link these packages.

### ooda opm

Delegate to the `opm` package manager.

```sh
ooda opm add foo
ooda opm audit
ooda opm launch --exec foo
```

Source: spawn `opm` at `$OODACODEX/bin/opm` only. Exit: whatever `opm` exits with. OODACODEX is required.

### ooda lsp

Delegate to the `lsp` LSP server.

```sh
ooda lsp                     # stdio mode (the editor case)
ooda lsp request.txt         # one-shot file mode
```

Source: spawn `lsp` at `$OODACODEX/bin/lsp` only. Exit: whatever `lsp` exits with. OODACODEX is required.

### ooda mcp

Delegate to the `mcp` MCP server.

```sh
ooda mcp                     # stdio mode
ooda mcp --file request.txt  # one-shot file mode
```

Source: spawn `mcp` via `$OODACODEX/bin/mcp` (stdio inherited). Exit: whatever `mcp` exits with. OODACODEX is required.

### ooda mcp-merge

Merge the openooda MCP server config into an MCP client config (Claude Desktop, Cursor, etc.). Default client: claude.

```sh
ooda mcp-merge --client claude
ooda mcp-merge --client cursor --dry-run
```

Source: spawn `mcp` with leading `mcp-merge` (not a separate binary). Exit: whatever `mcp` exits with.

### ooda version

Print the ooda binary version. Source of truth: `OODA_VERSION` env var; falls back to the build-time literal `v0.2.16` (acknowledged stale; refresh in next release).

```sh
ooda version
ooda --version
ooda -v
```

Source: `main.oo` (`version` dispatch). Exit: 0.

### ooda help

Print the help text. Triggered when `ooda help` is explicit, or when an unknown subcommand is given. Bare `ooda` opens ooda-tui.

```sh
ooda help
ooda unknown-cmd    # prints help + Err
```

Source: `main.oo` (`router_help`). Exit: 0 on explicit help; 2 on unknown subcommand.
